 The desktop shell frame on the real runtime -- H4's first rung. The
 guios desktop proved a 19-app shell in the emulator, but it leans on
 codex-vm devices no real machine has: a host-side triangle rasterizer
 at MMIO 0xBE000000 with doorbell ports 0x400-0x402, absolute mouse
 coordinates synthesized on ports 0xE1-0xE4, and frame pacing by
 port-224 VM exits. This chapter is the frame those apps will land on,
 built only from what the Option A runtime actually provides: the GOP
 framebuffer from the handoff cells, keyboard and mouse from the H2
 USB stack (or PS/2 through the same mailbox), the PIT tick cell for
 pacing, and the CMOS RTC for wall-clock time.

 There is no frame loop running at a made-up rate. The desktop is
 event-driven: the loop polls the keyboard mailbox and the mouse pump
 -- both allocation-free when idle -- and repaints exactly what an
 event dirtied. The clock redraws when the tick cell says a second
 has passed. A machine showing an idle desktop executes a poll loop
 that allocates nothing and writes nothing.

 We say:

Section: Palette and Layout

  dk-col-wall : Integer = #16213E
  dk-col-task : Integer = #0D1526
  dk-col-win : Integer = #223055
  dk-col-title : Integer = #2E5C8A
  dk-col-text : Integer = #909CB0
  dk-col-bright : Integer = #FFFFFF
  dk-col-green : Integer = #00FF00

  dk-task-h : Integer = 28
  dk-win-w : Integer = 360
  dk-win-h : Integer = 160
  dk-title-h : Integer = 20

  dk-win-x : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dk-win-x (w) (s) = (w - dk-win-w * s) / 2

  dk-win-y : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dk-win-y (h) (s) = (h - dk-task-h * s - dk-win-h * s) / 2

Section: RTC

 The CMOS RTC answers on ports 0x70/0x71 on every PC, virtual or
 real -- no VM convenience involved. Registers 0, 2, 4 are seconds,
 minutes, hours, BCD-encoded.

  rtc-read : Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  rtc-read (reg) = act
    w <- port-out-byte 112 reg
    port-in-byte 113
  end

  dk-bcd : Integer -> Integer
  dk-bcd (n) = (n / 16) * 10 + int-mod n 16

  dk-pad2 : Integer -> Text
  dk-pad2 (n) = if n < 10 then "0" & show n else show n

Section: Chrome

 The shell chrome built with the real widget system -- the same
 shapes GuiShell's shell-build-root produces: a sidebar column of app
 buttons pinned 160 wide, and a right-hand column of flexible content
 over a 24-pixel taskbar row. The compositor lays it out against the
 real panel rectangle and paints it in software; the buttons become
 live in a later rung.

 A panel is born flexible (wn-flex 1); chrome that owns a fixed edge
 must say so, or the row splits the panel with its flexible sibling.

  desk-sidebar : Integer -> WidgetNode
  desk-sidebar (dummy) =
    widget-set-flex (widget-set-min (widget-panel "sidebar" DirColumn 1 [widget-label "brand" "CODEX", widget-button "files" "Files", widget-button "editor" "Editor", widget-button "terminal" "Terminal", widget-button "monitor" "Monitor", widget-button "settings" "Settings"]) 160 0) 0

  desk-taskbar : Integer -> WidgetNode
  desk-taskbar (dummy) =
    widget-set-flex (widget-set-min (widget-panel "taskbar" DirRow 4 [widget-label "task-brand" "CODEX", widget-set-flex (widget-label "task-spacer" "") 1]) 0 24) 0

  desk-chrome : Integer -> WidgetNode
  desk-chrome (dummy) =
    widget-panel "root" DirRow 0 [desk-sidebar 0, widget-set-flex (widget-panel "right" DirColumn 0 [widget-set-flex (widget-panel "content" DirColumn 0 []) 1, desk-taskbar 0]) 1]

Section: Drawing

 Body text prefers the TrueType font read off the stick's own ESP;
 without one the CBF bitmap font stands in, and a status line names
 which is on the glass.

  desk-line : Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Integer, GopFont, Integer, Integer, Text, Integer -> Integer
  desk-line (base) (stride) (h) (font) (s) (tf) (x) (y) (t) (fg) =
    if tf.gf-ok then gfont-text tf base stride h x y t fg
    else gop-draw-text base stride font x y t fg s 0

  desk-window : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Integer, GopFont -> Integer
  desk-window (base) (w) (h) (stride) (font) (s) (tf) =
    let wx = dk-win-x w s
    in let wy = dk-win-y h s
    in let body = gop-fill-rect base stride wx wy (dk-win-w * s) (dk-win-h * s) dk-col-win
    in let title = gop-fill-rect base stride wx wy (dk-win-w * s) (dk-title-h * s) dk-col-title
    in let cap = gop-draw-text base stride font (wx + 6 * s) (wy + 2 * s) "Welcome" dk-col-bright s 0
    in let xbox = gop-draw-text base stride font (wx + dk-win-w * s - 14 * s) (wy + 2 * s) "x" dk-col-bright s 0
    in let l1 = desk-line base stride h font s tf (wx + 10 * s) (wy + 32 * s) "The Codex desktop frame on the bare runtime." dk-col-text
    in let l2 = desk-line base stride h font s tf (wx + 10 * s) (wy + 52 * s) "Input arrives over USB HID or PS/2; the clock" dk-col-text
    in let l3 = desk-line base stride h font s tf (wx + 10 * s) (wy + 72 * s) "runs on PIT ticks and the CMOS RTC. No emulator" dk-col-text
    in let l4 = desk-line base stride h font s tf (wx + 10 * s) (wy + 92 * s) "devices, no frame pacing, no font disk." dk-col-text
    in let l5 = desk-line base stride h font s tf (wx + 10 * s) (wy + 108 * s) (if tf.gf-ok then "Font: TrueType CMUNSS.TTF from this stick's ESP." else "Font: CBF bitmap (no TTF on the ESP).") dk-col-bright
    in desk-line base stride h font s tf (wx + 10 * s) (wy + 128 * s) "Files (or f) browses this stick. Esc returns to the menu." dk-col-green

 The bounded tree comes back to the caller: it is the hit-test map
 that makes the sidebar buttons live.

  desk-draw : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Integer, GopFont -> WidgetNode
  desk-draw (base) (w) (h) (stride) (font) (s) (tf) =
    let laid = comp-render base stride font (desk-chrome 0) theme-terminal w h
    in let win = desk-window base w h stride font s tf
    in laid

 The clock sits at the right end of the widget taskbar (24 pixels,
 bottom of the panel), painted in the taskbar's own theme colors so a
 redraw leaves no seam.

  desk-draw-clock : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Text -> Integer
  desk-draw-clock (base) (w) (h) (stride) (font) (t) =
    let st = resolve-state (theme-terminal.th-panel) 0
    in let tw = text-length t * 8
    in let tx = w - tw - 8
    in let ty = h - 24 + 4
    in let bg = gop-fill-rect base stride tx ty tw 16 (st.ws-bg)
    in gop-draw-text base stride font tx ty t (st.ws-fg) 1 0

Section: Clock Gate

 One RTC read per second, gated by the PIT tick cell the runtime-init
 spine keeps counting (cell 28672, ~18 ticks per second). Between
 seconds the gate is two peeks and a compare.

  desk-clock : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  desk-clock (base) (w) (h) (stride) (font) (ds) = act
    let now = peek-32 28672 0
    in if now - peek-32 ds 8 < 18 then 0
    else act
      hh <- rtc-read 4
      mm <- rtc-read 2
      ss <- rtc-read 0
      let st = poke-32 ds 8 now
      in desk-draw-clock base w h stride font (dk-pad2 (dk-bcd hh) & ":" & dk-pad2 (dk-bcd mm) & ":" & dk-pad2 (dk-bcd ss))
    end
  end

Section: Hit Testing

  desk-close-hit : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  desk-close-hit (w) (h) (s) (mx) (my) =
    let wx = dk-win-x w s
    in let wy = dk-win-y h s
    in let bx = wx + dk-win-w * s - 16 * s
    in if mx < bx then False
    else if mx >= wx + dk-win-w * s then False
    else if my < wy then False
    else if my >= wy + dk-title-h * s then False
    else True

Section: Loop

 Esc or a left-click on the close box leaves the desktop and returns
 to the caller (the boot menu). The self tail call keeps the loop
 constant-stack; the pet flag build keeps the watchdog quiet.

 Widget hit: the click point resolved against the bounded tree the
 compositor returned. Only the Files button is live today; a click
 on an id with no app behind it is a click on inert chrome.

  desk-widget-hit : WidgetNode, Integer, Integer, Text -> Boolean
  desk-widget-hit (root) (mx) (my) (id) =
    when ev-hit-widget root mx my
      is Just (wgt) -> wgt.wn-id == id
      is None -> False

 Returning from an app repaints the whole desktop. The cursor hides
 BEFORE the repaint (restore then clear -- clearing alone bakes the
 old cursor pixels into the next saved patch wherever the repaint
 does not cover them) and is re-placed after.

  desk-files : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, GopFont, UsbKbd, UsbMouse, Integer, Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  desk-files (base) (w) (h) (stride) (font) (tf) (kbd) (mouse) (ds) (cs) = act
    r <- gfl-run base w h stride font kbd mouse cs
    hd <- cursor-hide cs base stride
    let root = desk-draw base w h stride font (ui-scale w) tf
    in let c0 = if mouse.um-ok then cursor-update cs base stride w h (ui-scale w) (mouse-x mouse) (mouse-y mouse) else 0
    in desk-loop base w h stride font tf kbd mouse ds cs root
  end

  desk-loop : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, GopFont, UsbKbd, UsbMouse, Integer, Integer, WidgetNode -> [Device.Port] Integer
  desk-loop (base) (w) (h) (stride) (font) (tf) (kbd) (mouse) (ds) (cs) (root) = act
    sc <- kbd-take kbd
    ck <- desk-clock base w h stride font ds
    let mv = mouse-pump mouse w h
    in let cu = if mv == 1 then cursor-update cs base stride w h (ui-scale w) (mouse-x mouse) (mouse-y mouse) else 0
    in let clicked = mv == 1 & mouse-clicked mouse
    in let closed = clicked & desk-close-hit w h (ui-scale w) (mouse-x mouse) (mouse-y mouse)
    in let files = if sc == 33 then True else clicked & desk-widget-hit root (mouse-x mouse) (mouse-y mouse) "files"
    in if sc == 1 then 0
    else if closed then 0
    else if files then desk-files base w h stride font tf kbd mouse ds cs
    else desk-loop base w h stride font tf kbd mouse ds cs root
  end

 The TrueType face comes off the boot medium through the same mount
 every storage screen uses; a stick without one leaves gf-ok False
 and the desk speaks CBF.

  desk-font : Integer -> [Device.Port] GopFont
  desk-font (dummy) = act
    m <- gfat-mount-esp
    if m.gm-ok == False then gfont-none
    else gfont-load (m.gm-vol) "CMUNSS.TTF"
  end

  desk-run : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, UsbKbd, UsbMouse -> [Device.Port] Integer
  desk-run (base) (w) (h) (stride) (font) (kbd) (mouse) = act
    tf <- desk-font 0
    let s = ui-scale w
    in let ds = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in let cs = alloc-zeroed 2048 64
    in let wp = mouse-warp mouse (w / 2) (h / 2)
    in let root = desk-draw base w h stride font s tf
    in let c0 = cursor-update cs base stride w h s (w / 2) (h / 2)
    in desk-loop base w h stride font tf kbd mouse ds cs root
  end
